{title: 411 - The Son of God Proclaim}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #411 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 411}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]The [F]Son of [Bb]God [Gm]proclaim,
[F/A]The [Bb]Lord of [Gm]time [C]and space;
[Dm]The [Bb]God [Dm]who bade [Am/C]thelight [Gm]break [C]forth
[Am]Now [Dm]shines [Am]in [C7]Je sus’ [F]face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Behold [F/A]His [Bb]out [Gm]stretched [C7]hands,
[F/A]Though [Bb]all was [F/A]in [Gm]His [C]power
[Dm]He took [Bb]the [Dm]towel [Am/C]and [Bb]basin [C]then,
[Am]And [Dm]serves [Am]us [C7]in this [F]hour.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]He, [F]God's creative [Gm]word,
[F/A]The [Bb]church's [F/A]Lord [Gm]and [C]head,
[Dm]Here [Bb]bids [Dm]us gather [Bb]as [Gm]His [C]friends,
[Am]And [Dm]share His [Am]wine [C7]and bread.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]The [F]Lord of [Bb]life [Gm]and [C7]death
[F/A]With [Bb]wondering [Gm]praise [C]we sing;
[Dm]We [Bb]break [Dm]the bread [Am/C]at [Bb]His [Gm]command,
[Am]And [Dm]name Him [Am]God [C7]and King.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]We [F]take this [Bb]cup [Gm]in [C7]hope:
[F/A]For [Bb]He, who [Gm]gladly [C]bore
[Dm]The shameful cross, [Am/C]is [Bb]ris'n [Gm]again,
[Am]And [Dm]reigns forevermore.
{end_of_verse}
